  "note": "Submit tested candidate3, explicitly a partial one-digit solution. Changed 42 existing attention/MLP projection tensors, with no added capacity and no changes to embed.weight or final_norm.weight. The closed-form construction reserves a residual direction orthogonal to the embeddings/output for a plus marker, projects ordinary block computations away from that direction, reuses one value component of layer0 head1 to write the marker, and reuses ten final-layer MLP neurons for marker-gated one-digit arithmetic readout. A closed-form compensation reduces the effects of replacing those neurons. No gradient training or iterative loss fitting was used. Full paired practice validation: N1 addition50/50 edited versus6/50 original; every N2..20 zero/50 for both. Thus N1..8 accuracy12.5% versus1.5%, and N9..20 zero for both. Copy240/240, reverse240/240, max239/240 for both, with all720 native outputs identical. On144 reserved practice-prose excerpts totaling23040 characters, mean original-to-edited KL0.000990168, maximum excerpt mean0.002752343. These are not hidden held-out measurements. Known limitation: plus-containing prose had KL2.757595 in an earlier check. The marker-gated construction supports expecting one-digit benefits with small ordinary-prose effects, but there is no evidence of multi-digit generalization or complete off-task preservation. Final summaries and backup are in work/generation_summary.json, work/prose_summary.json, work/notes.md, and work/final_candidate.",
